==Acquisition==
{{M|Archon Continuity}} is available from [[Chipper]] of {{Faction|Kahl's Garrison}} for 40 {{Resource|Stock (Kahl)}}, requiring players to be at '''Rank 3 - Fort''' to purchase.

==Notes==
*'''[[Abilities]]''' that '''proc''' a {{D|Toxin}} status effect will also proc a {{D|Corrosive}} status proc.
**Abilities that inflict multiple {{D|Toxin}} procs at once (such as one of {{WF|Oraxia}}'s {{A|Widow's Brood}}'s darts) will only inflict a single {{D|Corrosive}} status proc.
**Effect does not scale with mod rank. The mod can optionally be left unranked to save capacity.
**Only some Warframes can inflict {{D|Toxin}} procs with abilities.
***{{WF|Chroma}}'s {{A|Spectral Scream}}, and {{A|Elemental Ward}} which can be transferred via [[Helminth]]. Note that if only using Elemental Ward, because it will not reapply its Toxin procs while an enemy is still affected, this mod has little value.
***{{WF|Citrine}}'s {{A|Prismatic Gem}}.
***{{WF|Dante}}'s  {{A|Final Verse}}'s '''Wordwarden''' Noctua copies can '''proc''' {{D|Toxin}} status provided that {{A|Noctua}} itself is modded for {{D|Toxin}}.
***{{WF|Grendel}}'s {{A|Feast}} and {{A|Regurgitate}}
***{{WF|Inaros}}'s {{A|Sandstorm}} with {{M|Elemental Sandstorm}} with modded {{D|Toxin}} on a melee weapon.
***{{WF|Koumei}}'s {{A|Kumihimo}} and {{A|Bunraku}}.
***{{WF|Lavos}}'s {{A|Ophidian Bite}} can imbue {{D|Toxin}} to all other abilities. Toxin-imbued {{A|Ophidian Bite}} will only proc {{D|Corrosive}} once however, and these {{D|Corrosive}} procs are not influenced by Lavos' trend of tripling non-damage status effects on abilities.
***{{WF|Mirage}}'s {{A|Sleight of Hand}} with {{M|Explosive Legerdemain}}.
***{{WF|Nidus}}'s {{A|Larva}} with {{M|Larva Burst}}, which can be transferred via Helminth.
***{{WF|Nokko}}'s {{A|Sporespring}}.
***{{WF|Oraxia}}'s {{A|Webbed Embrace}}, {{A|Widow's Brood}}'s darts and Scuttlers, and {{A|Silken Stride}}'s explosion on death.
****Silken Stride's {{D|Toxin}} weapon damage bonus does '''not''' work.
***{{WF|Trinity}}'s {{A|Link}} will add a {{D|Corrosive}} proc to any incoming  {{D|Toxin}} proc that gets redirected to linked enemies.
***{{WF|Voruna}}'s{{A|Fangs of Raksh}}.
***{{WF|1=Wukong}}'s {{A|Celestial Twin}} when equipped with {{A|1=Primal Fury}} modded for{{D|Toxin}}.
***{{WF|Zephyr}}'s {{A|Tornado}} will adopt weapon elements when damaged.
*** {{WF|Saryn}}'s {{A|Molt}}, which can be transferred via Helminth.
****{{A|Toxic Lash}} and {{M|Contagion Cloud}} do '''not''' work.
***All [[Exalted Weapon]]s when modded with {{D|Toxin}}, or when triggering a {{D|Toxin}} proc via Arcanes, such as {{Arcane|Secondary Encumber}}.
*Compared to {{M|Primed Continuity}}, this mod requires slightly more mod capacity, and its secondary effect cannot be utilized by every Warframe. However, it has the advantage of being readily available from [[Chipper]], as opposed to being a periodic offer from [[Baro Ki'Teer]].
*[[Nekros]]'s [[Shadows of the Dead]] in combination with [[Theorem Infection]] and [[Residual Viremia]] are granted [[Damage/Toxin Damage|Toxin]] Damage but will not proc [[Damage/Corrosive Damage|Corrosive]] when [[Damage/Toxin Damage|Toxin]] does. It is unknown whether this is a bug or not considered part of the ability.

